# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# The router also handles these paths (see src/routes/AppRoutes.jsx), but a
# client-side <Navigate> is a 200 with a JavaScript hop — a crawler sees the
# old URL return successfully and has no signal that the page moved. These
# rules answer with a real 301 before the SPA ever loads, which is what
# actually transfers ranking to the new URL.
#
# The in-app routes stay as a fallback for anyone already inside the app,
# and for local development where this file is not served.

/ats-resume-checker            /resume-checker            301
/career-tools/linkedin         /linkedin-optimization     301
/career-tools/cover-letter     /cover-letter-generator    301
/career-tools/interview        /interview-preparation     301
/dubai-job-seeker-package      /dubai-launch              301
/documentation                 /appostle-services         301
/employer                      /employers                 301

# Query strings are preserved by Pages, so /documentation?category=Apostille
# lands on /appostle-services?category=Apostille without a second rule.

# SPA fallback: every other path is served the shell so the router can
# resolve it. This must stay last — rules are matched in order.
/*                             /index.html                200
